-- TITAN V1.6.3 — Contrôle et réconciliation. Applies after 20261123090000 (V1.6.2). Additive: two functions for the account owner and
-- one private helper; the public wrapper of the session edit gains one guard. No table, no column, no grant on a table; reward and
-- record rules unchanged. NOT APPLIED TO PRODUCTION by the session that wrote it: it needs the owner's release approval.
--
-- 1. « Ce qui a changé » : every correction, archive and restore already stores the previous row in public.training_revisions
--    (private.titan_update_training_session), exported by « Exporter toutes mes données » (trainingRevisions), but no client could read
--    it. public.titan_session_changes_v1(log id) returns, for the owner only, the 50 latest changes of one session, newest first:
--    { revision, at, changes: [{ field, before, after, unit }] } with the fields the clients word the same way
--    (js/core/history-ledger.js changeText): val (with the unit), unit, date (to the minute), duration, note, archived.
-- 2. A restore must never count the same effort twice. When the athlete rejoined an import to their session (V1.6.2 « Même séance »),
--    the session the split had created is archived and the import counts through the athlete's session. Restoring that archived
--    session from the journal would put both back in totals and records while the link still says « même séance ». The journal
--    restore of such a session is refused with SESSION_MATCH_JOINED (22023): « Séparer » in « Sources » is the way back, it restores
--    the same session and records the decision (titan_resolve_session_match_v1 calls the private function, not this wrapper).
